From: kria-fde build <patch@local>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: pkcs7_verify: drop X.509 signing-time validity check

The EFI secure-boot image verification path (legacy crypto backend) calls
pkcs7_verify_one(), which rejects a signature whose embedded PKCS#7
signingTime authenticated attribute falls outside the signing
certificate's [valid_from, valid_to] window ("Message signed outside of
X.509 validity window", -EKEYREJECTED).

This causes otherwise-valid images to fail authentication whenever the
signing certificate has expired (or is not yet valid) relative to the
time the image was signed, even though the board has no trusted wall
clock. Remove the check so authentication depends only on the signature
chaining to a trusted key in db, not on certificate validity dates.

Applies to U-Boot v2025.01 / Xilinx xlnx_rebase_v2025.01_update
(tag xlnx_rebase_v2025.01_2025.1_update1).

Signed-off-by: kria-fde build <patch@local>
---
 lib/crypto/pkcs7_verify.c | 12 ------------
 1 file changed, 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/crypto/pkcs7_verify.c b/lib/crypto/pkcs7_verify.c
index 9d7b9f6bce8..af2e9ebdfa5 100644
--- a/lib/crypto/pkcs7_verify.c
+++ b/lib/crypto/pkcs7_verify.c
@@ -526,18 +526,6 @@ static int pkcs7_verify_one(struct pkcs7_message *pkcs7,
 	pr_devel("Using X.509[%u] for sig %u\n",
 		 sinfo->signer->index, sinfo->index);

-	/* Check that the PKCS#7 signing time is valid according to the X.509
-	 * certificate.  We can't, however, check against the system clock
-	 * since that may not have been set yet and may be wrong.
-	 */
-	if (test_bit(sinfo_has_signing_time, &sinfo->aa_set)) {
-		if (sinfo->signing_time < sinfo->signer->valid_from ||
-		    sinfo->signing_time > sinfo->signer->valid_to) {
-			pr_warn("Message signed outside of X.509 validity window\n");
-			return -EKEYREJECTED;
-		}
-	}
-
 	/* Verify the PKCS#7 binary against the key */
 	ret = public_key_verify_signature(sinfo->signer->pub, sinfo->sig);
 	if (ret < 0)
--
2.43.0
